 "description": "OpenRouter is an AI \"model exchange\": a single, OpenAI-compatible API endpoint that routes requests to hundreds of language models from dozens of providers, handling billing, provider selection, and automatic fallback. Founded in 2023, it publishes a public rankings page counting prompt plus completion tokens per model variant, binned into daily UTC buckets, excluding requests users mark private. The data is CC BY 4.0 and available as JSON.\n\nVolume has grown steeply. At its May 2026 Series B (\\$113M led by CapitalG, \\~\\$1.3B valuation), OpenRouter reported roughly 25T tokens/week, up 5x from about 5T/week six months earlier. For the week ending September 13, 2026, the top ten models alone totaled 127T tokens\n\nCommonly cited drivers include agentic and coding workloads, aggressive pricing from open-weight models, and free model variants. OpenRouter notes the rankings measure adoption on its platform only, not the broader market.\n\nForecasters may want to consider whether compounding continues, plateaus, or reverses, and how holiday-week developer activity affects late-December bins.",
 "resolution_criteria": "This question will resolve as the number of tokens used through OpenRouter during the week of December 21-27, 2026, as reported by the [\"Top Models: Weekly usage of models across OpenRouter\" graph](https://openrouter.ai/rankings#top-models).",
 "fine_print": "The value displayed for the December 21 bar in the linked OpenRouter usage chart, including its displayed rounding, will be used for resolution. OpenRouter currently bins the chart into weeks running Monday through Sunday, so it is expected that a bar will cover December 21–27, 2026. If OpenRouter changes the bins to start on a different day, this question will resolve using the last full week falling within 2026.\n\nFor example, the equivalent question for September 7-13, 2026 would resolve to 127 trillion tokens:\n\n![](https://cdn.metaculus.com/user_uploaded/Screenshot_2026-09-14_at_3.17.36PM.png)"
